# _attach/exec scope 0 — run a command the other chassis asked for.
#
# This stack is what `txco attach` runs. A request comes down the link from
# the chassis this machine is attached to, and the link hands it here as
# data: the workspace exec that chassis's stack made, under @attach.req, and
# the credential it came in under, at @attach.credential. Every request
# enters this stack; nothing in a request can choose another.
#
# The exec below runs on THIS machine, through the owner workspace provider:
# as you, with your environment, starting in the folder `txco attach <code>`
# was run in. The workspace is named by the credential, which is how two
# attached workspaces on one machine each get their own folder.
#
# What the link sends back is `.attach` (and `.workspace.error`, when the
# exec could not run at all). Nothing else of this run leaves the machine.
#
# It is yours to change. Put a file of the same name under
#   <txco home>/attach/OPS/_attach/exec/0/
# to replace this rule, or one of another name, in this scope or another, to
# add to it: a log line, a command policy, an environment. Only this stack
# can run commands here.
#
# @ is sugar for ._txc.
WHEN @src == "attach" && @attach.req.shell == true
  WITH workspace = @attach.credential,
       command   = @attach.req.command,
       stdin     = @attach.req.stdin,
       cwd       = @attach.req.cwd,
       env       = @attach.req.env,
       timeout   = @attach.req.timeout_ms,
       detach    = @attach.req.detach,
       into      = "attach"
  EXEC "workspace://machine/exec"
